.TH LOAD 1.SH NAMEload \- load modules into memory.SH SYNOPSIS\fBload\fR[\-dl] [\-z[=file]] module ....SH DESCRIPTION\fBload\fRreads each module file named into memory and enters it in the moduledirectory, so that a program that links a module by name finds it:\fBload /dd/CMDS/os9lib\fRis what brings the RTF Fortran set to life..PPThis is a clean-room reimplementation of Microware's\fBload\fR,\fRwritten from the published manuals so that the collection can stand onits own; the source is\fBSRC/load\fR.\fR.SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-d\fRlook for the file in the data directory rather than the executiondirectory..TP 12\fB\-l\fRprint the pathlist of each file loaded..TP 12\fB\-z\fRread the names from the standard input, or with\fB\-z=\fIfile\fRfrom\fIfile\fR.\fR.SH NOTESYour own OS-9 has Microware's\fBload\fR;\fRsee\fBDOC/README-NAMES\fRfor which one a bare\fBload\fRruns..SH SEE ALSOunlink, mdir